Hand clippy the rustc environment the command line adds

The clippy aspect takes the extra_rustc_flag setting but not extra_rustc_env,
so a variable set there for every rustc action, such as RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP, is
missing from clippy's, and clippy may then lint under other cfgs than the
compile.

The patch adds three lines to the aspect's attributes and carries the six
around them, too little of the file to attribute.

License: Apache-2.0 (hermeticbuild/rules_rust source-fd521efe16c03e4cd169453eb44fb98d73ebb7aa)

--- a/rust/private/clippy.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/clippy.bzl
@@ -349,6 +349,9 @@
             doc = "The desired `--error-format` flags for rustc",
             default = "//rust/settings:error_format",
         ),
+        "_extra_rustc_env": attr.label(
+            default = Label("//rust/settings:extra_rustc_env"),
+        ),
         "_extra_rustc_flag": attr.label(
             default = Label("//rust/settings:extra_rustc_flag"),
         ),
